+      "type": "text",
+      "title": "Choosing between tú and usted",
+      "content": "*Tú* is for people you are close to: family, friends, classmates, children. *Usted* shows respect or distance: strangers, older people, customers, someone senior at work. *Usted* takes the same verb form as *él* and *ella*. The line moves from place to place: in parts of Colombia and in Costa Rica, people also use *usted* with family and close friends. Usually the older person, or the one with more authority, is the one who offers *tú*."
