     },
+    {
+      "type": "text",
+      "content": "*No cabe duda de que* is a strong, formal way to say \"there is no doubt\". It takes the indicative, because you present the fact as certain. In the same way *no dudo que* takes the indicative: *No dudo que viene*. Doubting is the other side: *dudo que* and *no es seguro que* take the subjunctive. The rule is the one from B2 Unit 3: a fact you present as certain takes the indicative, and a doubt takes the subjunctive."
+    },
     {
       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "El empleo del condicional compuesto ('habría cabido esperar', 'habría sido deseable') permite formular balances retrospectivos críticos con exquisita elegancia diplomática."
