-        ]
+      "type": "text",
+      "title": "Three devices",
+      "content": "A metaphor says that one thing *is* another, without *como*: *El tiempo es un río* does not mean time has water; it means time flows and does not come back. With *como* it is a comparison, not a metaphor: *El tiempo pasa como un río*. A rhetorical question is asked to make a point, not to get an answer: *¿Quién puede negar que los precios suben?* means \"nobody can deny it\". Repetition puts the same word in a row to stress an idea: *Trabajo, trabajo y más trabajo: así se aprende.*"
